# Second worked example, run inside real ChimeraX.
#
#   ChimeraX --nogui --silent --exit --script tests/integration/characterise_1acb.cxc
#
# 1ACB: alpha-chymotrypsin (E) with eglin c (I). A protease-inhibitor complex,
# so a different interface chemistry from barnase-barstar — larger, with the
# inhibitor loop inserted into the active site rather than a charged patch
# meeting a charged patch.
#
# It exists because until now every worked number in the manuscript came from
# one complex. 1ACB and 3SGB are already used for the PRODIGY cross-validation
# in section 3.1, so a second end-to-end example costs no new data.
#
# Expected, from the prodigy-prot cross-validation (Data S1):
#   contact terms at 5.5 A ... 72 pairs, CC 3 / CP 2 / AC 19 / PP 4 / AP 19 / AA 25
#   dG ...................... -12.18 kcal/mol (reference -11.9)
#
# One caveat specific to this entry, worth knowing before comparing to a
# prediction: the crystal is nicked, mature chymotrypsin. Chain E has breaks at
# 13->16 and 146->149 where the activation dipeptides were excised, so 241
# residues are observed against a 245-residue SEQRES. Predictors build the
# continuous chain from SEQRES. The interface is unaffected, but the two are
# not the same molecule.

close all
open 1acb

molcompose capabilities model #1
molcompose interface E I model #1 distance 4.5
molcompose interactions model #1
molcompose buriedarea model #1
molcompose affinity model #1
molcompose hotspots model #1 top 12

# The one-call path must agree with the individual commands above.
molcompose characterise E I model #1

molcompose report /private/tmp/molcompose-1acb-report.md model #1 format md
